# Use `repomap` for repository intelligence

This project has [`repomap`](https://github.com/karanjasani/agentkit) available: a
read-only, deterministic Go analysis CLI that emits stable JSON. Prefer it over
`grep`/`find` for structural questions.

## Instead of grepping, locate symbols

- `repomap symbol <Name> --signature-only` — signature + `file:line`.
- `repomap symbol <Name> --body` — full declaration source.
- `repomap symbol <Name> --doc` — doc comment only.
- `repomap struct <pkg.Type>` — recursive JSON contract of a type.

## Understand structure

- `repomap overview` — packages, entrypoints, generated/vendored code.
- `repomap package <path>` — imports, importers, exports, tests.
- `repomap deps <path>` — intra-module dependency graph.

## Trace relationships (edges carry a `confidence`)

- `repomap callers <Name>` — direct + indirect callers.
- `repomap tests <Name>` — tests that exercise a symbol.

## Before running tests, scope the change

Run `repomap impact --base <ref>` first. It maps changed files to affected
packages, flags public-API changes, and returns `recommended_tests`. Prefer
running those recommended tests over the entire suite.

## HTTP surface area

- `repomap endpoint <METHOD> <path>` — route → handler → upstreams.
- `repomap upstreams <path>` — outbound calls under a path.

## Notes

- Output is deterministic JSON on stdout; diagnostics go to stderr.
- Every result carries `file:line` evidence anchors — cite them.
- `repomap` is read-only and offline; it never mutates the repository.
